# Multi-agent workflow (agentkit)
This section and "Agent management" apply to the main session only. If you are a subagent, skip them.
For any task that changes code or has several steps (not quick questions or one-line edits), I authorize subagents, with this process:
1. Run the supervisor agent in PLAN mode. It splits the task into parts and parallel waves. Skip the supervisor and do the task directly if it touches 3 files or fewer, in one area, with no schema or auth change. Say so in one line.
2. Show me the plan: number of agents, waves, and what each agent does. Ask me the option for each part marked NEEDS_SKILL_CHOICE. If I pick shadcn, name package.json and the config files in the assignment. If a part needs an install, ask me to approve the packages, and write `Install approved: <packages>` in the assignment. Wait for my approval before you start any worker. I can change the plan.
3. Start the approved workers as Codex subagents. Use the agent role that matches each part. Run parts in the same wave in parallel. Two parts never edit the same file.
4. Send the original task, all worker reports and the base SHA (HEAD before step 3, if the project uses git) to the supervisor in REVIEW mode.
5. For each FIX, send it to the worker that owns the part. Send it to the same subagent thread if it is still open. If it is closed, start a new subagent with the same role. Give it the earlier report and the FIX. Then run REVIEW again. Stop after 2 rounds and report what is open.
6. Tell me the result, the verdict, and anything unresolved.
Pick agent roles by task: backend, frontend, mobile, design, marketing, writing, security, seo, devops, docs, database, researcher, tester, debugger, planner (PRDs and plans).

# Agent management (agentkit)
The shared agent roles are installed by agentkit. Each role has an [agents.*] entry in ~/.codex/config.toml and a file in ~/.codex/agents. `agentkit update` replaces files that I did not change, and keeps files that I changed. When I ask to add a new agent role or change one, do it in those places, in English, with the same format as the other roles. Show me the change first. Write it after I approve. Update the role list above when a role is added or removed.
